{"format_version":1,"partition":21774,"records":{"bosna":{"entries":[["bosna",null,"/ˈbɔsna/",null,{"g":"f","decl":"||||s|s|s|s"}]],"senses":[[6855,"bosna","noun","a fast-food snack consisting of a bratwurst in a bun, garnished with mustard and onions, and noticeably spicier than an American-style hot dog",0,"f",["Austria","Bavaria","Southern"]]]},"bügel":{"entries":[["bügel",null,"/ˈbyːɡəl/","From Middle High German *bügel (attested as bügele f, later bogell m [15th c.]), from Proto-Germanic *bugilaz, from the root of *beuganą (“to bend, bow”). Cognate with Dutch beugel, Middle Low German bȫgel (earlier already Old Saxon armbugil), Old Norse bygill (whence Danish bøjle etc.).\nIt seems that the word was originally northern (Low and Central German) and established itself more widely only during the 16th century. The Schweizerisches Idiotikon still considers it “not truly autochthonous” (nicht recht volksmäßig).",{"g":"m","decl":"|||s|||n|"}]],"senses":[[17967,"bügel","noun","a bent or curved piece of metal (or less often other material), a bail, bow, ring, specifically",0,"m"],[17968,"bügel","noun","a handle such as that of a bucket",1,"m"],[17969,"bügel","noun","an arm of glasses",2,"m"],[17970,"bügel","noun","ellipsis of Kleiderbügel: clothes hanger",3,"m"],[17971,"bügel","noun","ellipsis of Steigbügel: stirrup",4,"m"],[17972,"bügel","verb","inflection of bügeln:",5],[17973,"bügel","verb","first-person singular present",6],[17974,"bügel","verb","singular imperative",7]],"related_forms":[[26931,"bügel","brillenbügel","derived"],[26932,"bügel","eimerbügel","derived"],[26933,"bügel","hemdbügel","derived"],[26934,"bügel","kleiderbügel","derived"],[26935,"bügel","steigbügel","derived"],[26936,"bügel","überrollbügel","derived"],[26937,"bügel","bügelbrett","derived"],[26938,"bügel","bügeleisen","derived"],[26939,"bügel","bügeleimer","derived"],[26940,"bügel","bügelschloss","derived"],[26941,"bügel","bügelstange","derived"],[26942,"bügel","beugen","related"],[26943,"bügel